# Package and read it

Packaging puts your chapters, cover and details into one EPUB file, the standard format for ebooks.

1. Click [Package EPUB]{.ui} at the top right. The [Share]{.ui} tab opens, with your book listed under [Download the EPUB]{.ui}.
2. Click [Read]{.ui}. Your book opens in a new browser tab, as a reader will see it.
3. Click [Download]{.ui} to save the EPUB file to your device.
4. Open the file in the reading app you use, such as Apple Books, Google Play Books or Thorium Reader.

Your book is now on your own shelf, beside every other ebook you have.

When you change the book, click [Package again]{.ui} and download the new file. The file you shared earlier does not change.

## What next

You have used every step a book needs. When you want to do more, the User Manual covers:

- starting from a sample book or an EPUB you already have
- adding pictures and changing how your book looks
- checking that every reader can use your book
- saving your book as a PDF for printing
